            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0164" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/8–2346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pawley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-23T20:00:00-03:00">August 23, 1946—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1495. Urtel 1959, August 3, noon.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d115-f1"/> I have approached Ambassador Gracie twice with reference
                    60,000 passenger car tires and 12,000 truck tires. Will see him again today on
                    this subject. Believe it undesirable this time to suggest Argentine Ambassador
                    here approach Foreign Office because Brazilian Foreign Office very much upset
                    with Argentine Govt regarding Argentina’s failure to fulfill its commitment with
                    reference delivery of wheat.</p>
                <p>(Deptel 1065, August 8, 8 p.m.).</p>
                <p>Sent to Buenos Aires; repeated to Dept.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pawley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
